From ef9a729424f45f9de253d034a9d40a2efdaeca49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?A=CC=82nderson=20Q?= <anquadros@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Jun 2026 14:09:38 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] terminal: Add per-terminal theme overrides

Let each terminal in a window carry its own theme, independent of the
window/global theme. TerminalView holds an optional resolved theme
override; TerminalElement reads the owning view's effective theme at its
two theme-capture points (prepaint and layout_grid) instead of the global
active theme, so panes in one window can render different themes without
mutating any global. layout_grid now takes the theme explicitly.

Adds theme: Terminal and theme: Clear Terminal actions. The theme
selector gains an optional apply-override callback so it can drive a
single terminal's theme (live preview, revert on dismiss, no settings
file write) while the global selection path is unchanged.

Per-terminal overrides are session-scoped (not persisted across restart).
